-{"id": "DB-GAP-048", "status": "in_progress", "priority": "P3", "complexity": 2, "title": "P3 — `s3 query` (DuckDB httpfs) does not honor AWS_PROFILE — requires direct AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/SECRET env", "reasoning": "Bunker staging evidence 09-17 (las-bunker-03): with AWS_PROFILE=duckbrain + AWS_ENDPOINT_URL set, `duckbrain s3 query` fails 'Authentication Failure - no credentials are provided' while the SAME shell succeeds at `aws s3 ls` (CLI honors the profile) and `duckbrain s3 status` works. Exporting AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY directly makes httpfs queries work immediately (90 rows read from s3:// read-only). Root cause class: DuckDB httpfs (secret manager) reads standard AWS_* env vars, not the ~/.aws/config profile chain git-remote-s3/boto3 use. So the s3 layer splits: git push/pull OK on profile, SQL-over-S3 needs direct keys. DX gap for profile-based installers (our own prod uses profiles). Fix direction: when only a profile is configured, resolve its creds via the AWS CLI/API at s3-query time and inject as temporary env, or document the direct-key requirement in s3 config output. Evidence transcript: bunker /tmp/vitest-bunker.log session, staging probe commands in tick 518 report.", "source": "kara-direct bunker staging 2026-09-17", "created_at": "2026-09-17T04:57:17.000000Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-20T01:26:00-05:00", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/duckbrain-DB-GAP-048", "branch": "wt/DB-GAP-048"}
