 {"id": "GAP-033", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "title": "LOAD-HYGIENE: bound test-suite host load (audit tests for parallel-spawn / per-assertion subprocess / unbounded-loop patterns; fix the worst offender with bounded waves or in-process coverage; keep full-suite coverage; NO skip-gates, NO fleet-scheduling changes) — fleet pattern evidence: task-router TR-077/TR-078 2026-09-19 (40-at-once interpreter stampede, 66 seed builds/run, full core)", "reasoning": "fleet load-hygiene directive (task-router TR-077/078 evidence, injected by task-router-load-audit 2026-09-19; left uncommitted for the owning foreman)", "detail": "Fleet directive (Bane, criterion 7 of the 2026-09-19 retirement loop): 1-2 projects must not eat the whole box's CPU; the foreman also won't run next processes under excess load. Proven fleet pattern from task-router 2026-09-19: a concurrency test fired 40 simultaneous interpreter spawns (fixed: bounded waves of 8, same contract, TR-078); a suite built 66 private seed registries per run (fixed: one shared session build for read-only consumers, private builds kept where inputs mutate, TR-077); missing pandas in a venv turned every seed into a full-core burn for minutes. ACCEPTANCE (audit-then-fix, in-repo only): (1) audit this repo's test suite for the three patterns: (a) tests spawning >8 concurrent subprocesses, (b) a subprocess per assertion where the process boundary is not the subject under test, (c) loops re-running an expensive builder per test when one shared build would cover read-only assertions; (2) fix the single WORST offender found (bound waves with an env knob clamped 2-16, or in-process + one real-exec parity smoke, or a session-scoped shared fixture + per-test copy); do NOT time-box, cache, or skip tests to pass; do NOT change fleet/scheduler concurrency policy (owner-set); (3) prove before/after with a concrete measurement (spawn count, wall clock, or peak concurrent children) recorded in the completion event; (4) full regression suite green after the change (in-flight runs are not passed). REFERENCE: task-router tests/conftest.py (shared_seed_registry/seed_registry_copy) and tests/test_circuit_hardening.py are the worked examples to copy from.", "ts": "2026-09-19T20:15:17Z", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/duckbrain-GAP-033", "branch": "wt/GAP-033", "completed_at": "2026-09-19T21:55:00Z", "commit_hash": "062fa82", "worker_status": "complete", "files_changed": "src/cli/token-roles.test.ts", "lines_added": "141", "lines_removed": "-69", "guard_result": "tier1 secrets+tests PASS; merged-tree gate 155/1212 unit + tsc 0 + prettier clean + INT 44/44; UI 38/38 + build 0", "ci_result": "pushed post-closeout; CI pending (batched-push run on pushed HEAD)", "judge_result": "tier1 PASS; tier2 PASS 78dc9a77 (re-judge completed after the wave tick; verdict .gitreins/history/2026-09-20/78dc9a77)", "foreman_note": "wave worker (tick duckbrain-2026-09-19-20-45-38), worktree /home/kara/worktrees/duckbrain-GAP-033, merged no-ff; judge tier1 PASS; tier2 PASS 78dc9a77 (verdict chain 6a2f7049 FAIL -> c2acd50d -> 3c01a3ac time-cap -> 78dc9a77 PASS; audit artifact ops/gap033-load-hygiene.md, measurement 5->1 spawns, 11.1s->1.52s); recovery tick 559 confirmed the merged-tree gate 155/1212 + full suite green."}
